  "summary": "Net::DNS versions through 1.55 for Perl allow remote execution injection via EDNS EXTENDED ERROR.",
  "details": "Net::DNS versions through 1.55 for Perl allow remote execution injection via EDNS EXTENDED ERROR.\n\nNet::DNS::RR::OPT::EXTENDED_ERROR::_decompose parses the EXTRA-TEXT field of an EDNS EXTENDED-ERROR option (RFC 8914) by tokenising the raw bytes and passing the result to Perl's eval. There is some escaping done for $ and @, but not for backticks. This can be exploited for command execution if $pkt->edns->option('EXTENDED-ERROR') is called in array context, for example with a payload of {0:`\"<command>\"`} in EXTRA-TEXT.",
  "severity": [
    {
      "type": "CVSS_V3",
      "score": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H"
    }
